```mermaid
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant App as Background Thread (main)
    participant Core as ARM Cortex-M4 Core
    participant Stack as Active Stack (MSP/PSP)
    participant NVIC as NVIC Controller
    participant ISR as Interrupt Handler (ISR)

    App->>Core: Executing normal background code
    Note over NVIC: Hardware peripheral asserts IRQ request line
    NVIC->>Core: Signals pending interrupt with priority evaluation
    Note over Core: Core finishes current instruction cycle
    
    Core->>Stack: Automatic Hardware Stacking (Push 8 registers):<br/>[xPSR, PC, LR, R12, R3, R2, R1, R0]
    Core->>Core: Loads EXC_RETURN magic code into LR (e.g. 0xFFFFFFF9)
    Core->>Core: Fetches ISR vector address from Vector Table (Flash/VTOR)
    Core->>Core: Switches from Thread Mode to Handler Mode (Privileged)
    
    Core->>ISR: Begins executing Interrupt Handler
    Note over ISR: User code handles event and clears peripheral pending flag
    ISR->>Core: Executes return instruction (`BX LR`) with EXC_RETURN
    
    Core->>Stack: Automatic Hardware Unstacking (Pop 8 registers):<br/>Restores [R0-R3, R12, LR, PC, xPSR]
    Core->>Core: Switches back to Thread Mode
    Core->>App: Resumes background thread execution seamlessly
```
